<%- include('../partials/head',{title:'Install ReLoop on your phone'}) %><%- include('../partials/public-nav') %>
<main class="public-page" id="mainContent">
 <section class="page-hero"><div class="public-container narrow"><span class="eyebrow light">RELOOP ON YOUR PHONE</span><h1>Your recycling workspace, one tap away.</h1><p>Install ReLoop from your mobile browser and launch it from your home screen. No APK or app-store account is required.</p></div></section>
 <section class="public-section"><div class="public-container narrow install-layout">
  <div class="install-highlight"><img src="/icons/reloop-192.png" width="72" height="72" alt="ReLoop app icon"><div><h2>ReLoop for mobile</h2><p>One account for customers, collectors and recycling partners.</p><div role="status" data-connection-status></div></div></div>
  <button class="btn primary install-cta" data-install-pwa type="button" hidden>Install ReLoop now</button><p class="install-help" data-install-status aria-live="polite">The install button appears here when your browser offers a direct install prompt. Otherwise follow the steps below.</p>
  <div class="install-grid"><article class="card install-step"><span class="badge">ANDROID</span><h2>Chrome or Samsung Internet</h2><ol><li>Open your ReLoop website on your phone over HTTPS.</li><li>Tap <strong>Install ReLoop now</strong> when offered, or use the browser menu <strong>⋮</strong>.</li><li>Select <strong>Install app</strong> or <strong>Add to Home screen</strong>, then confirm.</li><li>Open ReLoop using its new home-screen icon.</li></ol></article>
  <article class="card install-step"><span class="badge">IPHONE / IPAD</span><h2>Safari and supported iOS browsers</h2><ol><li>Open your ReLoop website in your browser.</li><li>Tap the <strong>Share</strong> button (square with an upward arrow).</li><li>Choose <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong> (or the install option shown by your iOS version).</li><li>Tap <strong>Add</strong> and launch ReLoop from your home screen.</li></ol><p>iOS does not support the same automatic install prompt as Android.</p></article></div>
  <div class="install-info"><h2>What works without internet?</h2><p>Only a small static interface and this offline explanation may load. Viewing private history, accepting jobs, submitting pickup updates and handling payments <strong>require internet</strong>. No offline changes are queued, and sensitive pages are not cached.</p></div>
  <div class="install-help"><a href="/login" class="btn secondary">Sign in</a> <a href="/register" class="btn secondary">Create account</a></div>
 </div></section></main><%- include('../partials/foot') %>
